# SCENARIO: fix_131_reload_cast_camera   SEED: 0   CAMERAS: auto   BOTCFG: off
# Fix #131 - a bot that was HIBERNATED when `/cavebot reload` ran is re-materialized from the DB
# (Game.loadBotPlayer) and reactivated awake, but hibernateBot had switched its broadcast off and
# reactivateBotForReload never switched it back on. It stayed in the cast list (getActiveBotNames),
# and castViewerLogin only wakes a bot it cannot FIND, so a camera got "This player is not
# broadcasting" until something hibernated and woke the bot (batch-1 #48 check, run b1_48, had to
# insert a `hibernate` before every post-reload camera login). reactivateBotForReload now restores
# the broadcast through the same helper activateBot and wakeBot use, and logs it:
# "Reactivated bot '<R>' for reload (...) cast=restored|kept".
# Run: runner.py fix_131_reload_cast_camera.steps --var R=<Thais bot>   (baseline bot: Kaelis Duke)
# The scenario starts and ends in debug mode with $R pinned (`reload debug,$R`), the usual harness
# precondition, so the hibernation loop cannot interfere and the reload only materializes $R.
# Acceptance:
#   - reload with $R HIBERNATED: the journal says "Reactivated bot '$R' for reload ... cast=restored",
#     and a camera login right after it SUCCEEDS without a wake in between (no "Woke bot '$R'"
#     journal line since that reload, no client login_error "not broadcasting");
#   - reload with $R AWAKE: "cast=kept", and the camera login succeeds again;
#   - every camera login produced a "[Cast] Viewer-N connected to $R" journal line.
# Baseline replay: replay.py on runs/b1_48 (old build) FAILS the cast=restored|kept checks (the
# reactivation line has no cast= field) and the no-wake check (the workaround's two wakes).
# The logins are optional=1 so the old build reports FAIL on the expects instead of a STUCK stop.
@srv cmd _global "reload debug,$R"
@srv sleep 20
# ---- case 1: hibernated at reload -> re-materialized from the DB ----
@srv cmd "$R" hibernate expect="hibernated"
@srv sleep 3
@srv cmd _global "reload debug,$R"
@srv sleep 20
@cam:$R login optional=1
@srv sleep 3
@cam:$R self optional=1
@cam:$R logout optional=1
@srv expect src=srv msg~="Reactivated bot '$R' for reload .* cast=restored" min=1 within=40
@srv expect src=srv k=cast_connect msg~="Viewer-[0-9]+ connected to $R " min=1 within=15
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Woke bot '$R'" within=35
@srv expect-none src=cli:* k=login_error err~="not broadcasting" within=35
# ---- case 2: awake at reload -> same Player, broadcast kept ----
@srv sleep 2
@srv cmd _global "reload debug,$R"
@srv sleep 20
@cam:$R login optional=1
@srv sleep 3
@cam:$R logout optional=1
@srv expect src=srv msg~="Reactivated bot '$R' for reload .* cast=kept" min=1 within=35
@srv expect src=srv k=cast_connect msg~="Viewer-[0-9]+ connected to $R " min=1 within=15
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Woke bot '$R'" within=30
@srv expect-none src=cli:* k=login_error err~="not broadcasting" within=30
@srv expect-none src=srv msg~="Lua Script Error" within=120
